WEBVTT

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.110
You won't use your ability even now?

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.490
To lose without even using Killing Art?

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.830
Please don't let that be your excuse.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.160
Otone!

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.340
Otone?

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.130
Seisa!

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.850
Otone, is this...?

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:42.850
I-I'm sorry... But Fujishiro
was just thinking of Eruna...

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.810
Wait, Otone!

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:49.740
Why? Why were you and Seisa fighting...?

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.620
Please wait, Seisa—

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.960
What's wrong? Say something.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.510
You don't have to hold back.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.300
Seisa...

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.850
Don't worry about me anymore.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.020
You made a new club with that girl, didn't you?

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:23.100
Congratulations. That's good enough, isn't it?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.270
Seisa, why are you—

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.480
Didn't I say not to worry about me?!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.110
Or...

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:36.660
Do you want to bear scars like this, too?

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.540
Let us go.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.040
What's wrong, Ichinomiya?

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.330
Akama!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.630
Oh, it's nothing, I've just been lost
in my delusions since this morning.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.470
I imagined winning the midterm battles,
and then having a harem!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.470
You're alone today? That's unusual.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.390
Mr. Bimii isn't around, either.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.060
Oh, now that you mention it—

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.890
No wonder my shoulder
felt so light this morning!

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.730
What is Mr. Bimii, your guardian angel, rowr?!

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:16.650
Well, I'm sure the teachers are busy
preparing for the midterm battles, too.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.860
Right?

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:21.240
Has the I'll Figure It Out Later Club
chosen a representative yet?

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:23.530
No, not yet...

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.450
It would make sense for the winner
of the rookie battle, Otone, to be the rep...

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:33.040
No, no, but Ichinomiya has gotten
a lot better recently, too!

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.380
Her special attack is super cool,
don't you think?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:47.220
Eruna...

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.230
What's the matter, Otone? You seem kind of down!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:51.770
Hm?

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.810
Fujishiro is always cheerful.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.560
Always 100% cheerful!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.400
Especially today, I'm three
times that, 300% cheerful.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:03.200
I have so much cheer that it's a problem.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:07.240
Then, I'm glad! Anyway, It's almost
time for the midterm battles.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:10.410
It'll be the I'll Figure It Out
Later Club's first official match!

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.160
We have to decide who'll be the club rep!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.250
Fujishiro does not want to be the club rep.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:16.710
Huh?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.380
Eruna, you should represent us.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:19.090
Hm?

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:25.890
I'm sure that would be better.
I mean, you formed this club for Seisa's sake.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.470
Otone?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.770
I apologize for yesterday. For going
out on my own and acting recklessly.

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.230
Fujishiro was wrong to do that.

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.900
I'm over that already!

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:38.770
I mean, you did that for me—

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.940
That might have been a lie.

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:41.940
Huh?

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:46.450
I said it was for you,
but it might have really been for myself.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:50.870
I might have been jealous of Seisa.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.040
But at least I know this is true—

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:57.250
Fujishiro wanted you to keep smiling.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:00.800
I admired the always-smiling Eruna...

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.380
That's why you should be
our representative, Eruna!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:07.970
Fight Seisa and show Fujishiro
your wonderful smile!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.600
Otone...

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.220
I-I think I said too much...

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:18.400
Well, Fujishiro will leave now. It's time to
give the thugs around town a talking to.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:20.940
Wait! I won't allow that.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:27.820
Even if I'm the representative, you're still a
member of the I'll Figure It Out Later Club.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:32.910
Help me with my training!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:41.130
I guess I have no choice.
But I won't hold back, so prepare yourself.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:50.180
Anticomplex!

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.510
Snake!

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.680
Toy Bayonet!

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:01.900
Very good.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:06.490
However, if you are satisfied with this,
you will not be able to beat Seisa.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.320
Huh?

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:14.620
At that time, Fujishiro only won
because Seisa didn't use Killing Art.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.670
If she used Killing Art,
Fujishiro would probably have lost.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.210
Really? But why didn't Seisa—

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.710
Oh, there you are!

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:28.720
Eruna! The tournament brackets
have been announced!

00:07:28.930 --> 00:07:31.890
I feel like this will be a wild year!

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:44.150
If we both advance smoothly, it looks like
we'll fight each other in the third round.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.030
Seisa's going home club is...

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.490
I cannot find the going home club.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:57.870
Oh, the going home club withdrew this time, too.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.750
But I'm glad because if we
had to go up against Seisa,

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.920
even Himi would have had a hard time.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:09.220
That's not true! I'm pretty strong, you know.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.890
If Seisa is as strong as
100,000 African elephants,

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:16.100
then I'm as strong as 100,000
ancient Naumann elephants!

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:17.310
Wow...

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:29.940
Killing Art.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.050
Sword.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.720
Why didn't you use Killing Art at that time?

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:15.200
Seisa! Please let me in! Seisa!

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:17.660
- Please have her go home.
- Seisa!

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:24.330
Seisa! Please let me in! Seisa! Seis—

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.750
Kurumi, where Seisa?

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.050
Please let me see her!

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:31.510
Please let me see Seis—

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.260
My lady said she does not want to see you.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.390
Please leave.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.760
Please, can't you do something?

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.100
I cannot do anything.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.350
Just one look!

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:41.770
Please leave.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:43.810
How annoying.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.360
She'd probably feel better
if she just fought head-on.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.360
Not like I can say anything
about other people, though.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:54.860
I'll give you this!

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:55.950
I don't want it.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.030
I'll add this, too!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:58.780
Please leave.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.200
Then, what about this? I was saving it!

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.000
My sleeping bag soaked with sweat and tears!

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:05.370
You're too persistent.

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:13.130
Even if I can't fight against Seisa,
what's important is winning and advancing.

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:17.640
If I do that, Seisa will acknowledge me one day.

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:20.600
Midterm battles, B-block, first round.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.310
I'll Figure It Out Later Club
rep, Eruna Ichinomiya,

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.690
versus broadcast club rep, Haruka Toishi.

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:28.940
Begin the match.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:32.980
Go...!

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:49.000
Good job making it past the first round!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.670
Congratulations!

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.880
Thanks! It was because
you helped me train, Otone!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:57.930
But that was White Otone
congratulating me just now, huh?

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.260
Do it again with Black Otone!

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:03.680
Huh? What are you, touched in the head?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.270
You just got past the first round.
There's nothing to congratulate you for.

00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.360
It's not even worth the "C" in congratulations.

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:11.650
Yeah, that! That!

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:15.280
You're not Otone without Black Otone!

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.650
This is no time to play around!

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.280
It's almost time for
Shigure and Kuzuryu's match.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.120
Shigure and Enoyan?

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.120
Let's go, Black Otone!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:31.000
How many times do I have to tell you? Fujishiro
isn't black or white! Fujishiro is pure white!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.380
You're not going to watch the match?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:42.640
I think that eejit's match is about to end.
At least the result—

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:43.850
Be quiet.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.530
My lady... Could it be...?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.080
What is this?

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.720
This is...

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.550
Seisa?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.850
It wasn't an optical illusion, was it?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.230
No, it might be what Usamaru saw the other day.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:46.030
Eruna isn't here yet...

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.700
I wonder what she's doing.

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:52.210
It's Shigure and Kuzuryu's first match
against each other, too. Jeez!

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:55.380
What? This is the first time
the two are fighting each other?

00:12:55.590 --> 00:13:00.670
Yeah. There have been so many official matches,
and they're both super strong,

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.090
but for some reason, the two of them
have never fought each other.

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:07.970
That's because Kuzuryu always ran away.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:12.390
When Kuzuryu knew that he would be
up against Shigure in the next match,

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.230
he always lost.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.910
This is kind of creepy...

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.870
Otone, are you a scaredy-cat?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:29.740
O-Of course not!

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.330
Fujishiro isn't scared of anything.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.370
If anything, something like a <i>manju</i>...

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.630
The photography club?

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:42.010
Now that you mention it, the photography
club seems like it would be a major club,

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.630
but I've never seen it.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:47.510
I don't think it was in
the tournament brackets either...

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.930
Wai... You're going in?!

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.850
Fujishiro isn't ready to go in yet...!

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:57.480
Eruna...

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:06.410
If you're scared, you can just wait there.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.890
Seisa...

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:48.360
These expressions on Seisa's face...

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:50.160
I've never seen her like that...

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.910
A beautiful sunset...

00:14:57.080 --> 00:15:00.790
It's like a picture...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.000
A picture?

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:18.940
Bimii?!

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:22.860
Oh, no!

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:24.940
Otone, you're late!

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.690
Where's Eruna?

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:29.990
Eruna disappeared into the
photography club's room...

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.700
And then, the door disappeared, too...!

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:36.080
Looks like something happened to Eruna.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:40.080
We should probably decide
things as quickly as possible.

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.880
Midterm battles, A-block, third round.

00:15:44.090 --> 00:15:46.840
Kyoma Kuzuryu versus Shigure Ninomiya.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:02.150
This is a different dimension from
the Mikagura Academy we were in, ryui.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:08.400
That's what I thought. That's why the sun will
never set no matter how much time passes.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:13.410
But this clubroom is one
that used to exist in the school, ryui.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.580
Seisa sealed it into a
different dimension with Killing Art

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:21.000
and made it into a room
that doesn't exist in reality, ryui.

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:23.210
Why would she do that...?

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:28.300
That's because Seisa was betrayed
terribly by an upperclassman she loved

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.800
in the photography club, ryui.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.720
The one who took this picture?

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:33.430
That's right.

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:37.770
It happened when Seisa was a first-year,

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.560
the day before the midterm battles, ryui.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.940
At the time, Seisa was in the art club.
The upperclassman was in the photography club.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:51.820
Seisa became a model for her photographs,
and the two became very close, ryui.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:57.540
Seisa respected her, and the
upperclassman loved Seisa like a little sister.

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:02.370
But in terms of battle ability,
Seisa was overwhelmingly stronger.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:05.710
And in the midterm battles that year,

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.670
she and Seisa were up against
each other in the first round, ryui.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:12.840
I didn't think I would be fighting you.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.840
I won't hold back.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.970
I don't expect you to. Let's have a fair fight.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:19.520
I'm looking forward to it!

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:23.980
Seisa didn't care about winning or losing.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.770
She was just happy to be able
to fight her upperclassman.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.860
Just like you right now, Eruna.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.490
But the upperclassman saw things differently, ryui.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:41.830
With Mikagura Academy's point system,
if you won, you'd get a lot of points and attention.

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:46.960
The upperclassman couldn't
lose to first-year Seisa, ryui.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.170
So...

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.510
Hey, Seisa, I have a favor to ask.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:52.840
Huh?

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.050
Will you throw tomorrow's match?

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.850
It was a simple thing.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:05.940
But if she did it, their relationship
up until then would be meaningless.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.110
That's why Seisa didn't
agree to her request, ryui.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.440
And so...

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.030
They had an unauthorized battle
the day before the official match.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.040
Of course, it was against the rules, ryui.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:24.250
The upperclassman may not
have meant for it to happen,

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:25.710
but in the end...

00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:36.340
Seisa was seriously injured, ryui...

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:39.180
The upperclassman dropped out
and left the school.

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.970
The photography club was disbanded...

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:45.890
And in order to erase her memories
with the upperclassman,

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:50.610
Seisa used Killing Art to seal off the
ruined school building and this clubroom,

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.820
and shut herself up in her mansion, ryui.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:56.570
Seisa...

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:02.370
But... But then why is it
coming back and disappearing...?

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:06.120
Seisa's power is probably weakening, ryui.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.380
That's why the space is becoming unstable...

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.920
I see, that's why...

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:16.300
It wasn't that Seisa didn't
use Killing Art on Otone,

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.340
she <i>couldn't</i> use it...!

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:26.850
No...!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.520
Even without using a power like Killing Art,

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:35.780
you just have to throw things away or burn them.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:41.490
Unless you are afraid to really get rid of them?

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:46.700
Even if things disappear from this world,
they continue to exist in our minds.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:49.710
And one day, they become memories.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:51.830
Isn't that good enough?

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.930
You're finally coming at me seriously, huh?

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.510
I've been waiting for this!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.560
What are you trying to sound
like an honor student for?

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:10.480
Are you saying that the school's hero
even cares about the delinquents?

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:12.310
I'm not an honor student!

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.060
I'm not a hero, either!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.480
I always admired you, Kyoma!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:20.240
The strong Kyoma who was
never bound by anything!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:30.660
Back then, you were always way above me.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.170
I always looked up to you.

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.340
Then I'll make you look up to me again!

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.380
So much so that your neck will hurt!

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:41.680
The manga hero that I admired fought
with his rival to become stronger.

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:43.930
That's how he became truly strong.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.640
This isn't a manga.

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:48.060
You really think things will go that smoothly?

00:20:49.230 --> 00:20:51.390
Hero Time!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.230
Palette Barrett!

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.110
Over here, Shigure.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:03.700
Part one, finished.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.410
End of the match.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.580
It's been a while since
I've had such an enjoyable battle.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.210
The manga hero I admired always shook
his opponent's hand like this after a fight

00:21:19.420 --> 00:21:22.930
and became friends with him.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:26.220
Well, we've always been friends, though.

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:37.730
I told you, this isn't a manga.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.400
Oh, we don't have time for this.

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.400
We have to save Eruna—

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:42.860
Huh?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.240
Eruna...!

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:47.780
I'm coming...!

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.580
What is this?

00:21:56.790 --> 00:22:00.800
Oh no, ryui!
Seisa's finally lost her power, ryui!

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:44.110
Kyoma, you finally did it. I knew you could.

00:23:44.320 --> 00:23:46.740
This is no time for that. Eruna's in trouble!

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:48.070
Actually, I'm fine.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:50.490
It's not much of a preview
if you tell them that!

00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:51.910
You've got to string them along,
even if it's a lie!

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:54.990
Next time, a trial awaits Eruna and I!

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:57.250
Will we be able to overcome
the numerous difficulties

00:23:57.450 --> 00:23:58.000
and manage to get marr—

00:23:58.210 --> 00:23:59.160
That's not it!

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.750
Next time, me and Seisa,
and Himi, and Otone, Katai, Rumina,

00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:07.630
and um, um, every cute girl
in the world have a wrestling—

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:09.550
That's not it either!

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:12.550
Okay then next time, Enoyan and
Minatogawa spend a fine spring day

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:16.010
on the north face of the Eiger
studying cave cricket ecol—

00:24:16.220 --> 00:24:17.640
Look, where are you even getting this from?!

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.850
You'll just have to watch,
and see what happens for yourself!

00:24:20.060 --> 00:24:21.770
Don't try to be clever about it!

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.980
Next time, it's the big final episode!
"Infinite Grand Finale"!

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.190
It's the last episode,
but I have a feeling it's a start!

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:32.820
Wait... You mean like,
"Our fight has only just begun"?!
